 _{ij} (\\xi _i-\\xi _j)(\\eta _i-\\eta _j)\\right] _{\\beta }^{\\mathrm{fGFF},0}. \\end{aligned}\n\n$$\\begin{aligned} {\\mathbb {P}}_\\beta ^{\\mathrm{UST}}[S] = \\left[ \\prod _{ij\\in S}\\beta _{ij} (\\xi _i-\\xi _j)(\\eta _i-\\eta _j)\\right] _{\\beta }^{\\mathrm{fGFF},0}. \\end{aligned}$$\n\n(B.5)\n\nFor the UST, it is well-known that negative association holds, i.e., that the occurrence of disjoint edges ij, kl are negatively correlated. Various proofs exist, see e.g. [23, 26]. We include a new proof that mimics the proof of the Ginibre inequality [24].\n\n### Proposition B.4\n\nFor the uniform spanning tree, negative association holds: for all distinct ij and kl,\n\n\\begin{aligned} {\\mathbb {P}}_\\beta ^{\\mathrm{UST}}[ij,kl] \\leqslant {\\mathbb {P}}_\\beta ^{\\mathrm{UST}}[ij]{\\mathbb {P}}_\\beta ^{\\mathrm{UST}}[kl]. \\end{aligned}\n\n$$\\begin{aligned} {\\mathbb {P}}_\\beta ^{\\mathrm{UST}}[ij,kl] \\leqslant {\\mathbb {P}}_\\beta ^{\\mathrm{UST}}[ij]{\\mathbb {P}}_\\beta ^{\\mathrm{UST}}[kl]. \\end{aligned}$$\n\n(B.6)\n\n### Proof\n\nConsider the doubled Grassman algebra \\Omega ^{4\\Lambda }$\\Omega ^{4\\Lambda }$ with generators \\xi _i,\\eta _i,\\xi '_i,\\eta '_i$\\xi _i,\\eta _i,\\xi '_i,\\eta '_i$ where i \\in \\Lambda '$i \\in \\Lambda '$. Abusing notation, we write \\langle \\cdot \\rangle $\\langle \\cdot \\rangle $ for the product of the two fGFF expectations, i.e.,\n\n\\begin{aligned} \\langle F(\\xi ,\\eta )G(\\xi ',\\eta ') \\rangle = \\langle F(\\xi ,\\eta ) \\rangle ^\\mathrm{fGFF,0}\\langle G(\\xi ,\\eta ) \\rangle ^\\mathrm{fGFF,0}. \\end{aligned}\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nProbability On Trees PDF | PDF | Vertex (Graph Theory) | Graph Theory (https://fr.scribd.com/document/356125959/PROBABILITY-ON-TREES-pdf)\nciteturn1search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10.0 years ago; Crawled: 1.2 years ago; conjectured this, Feder and Mihail (1992) proved it: ... Proof. ... (Negative Associa